Supplementary Materials for [Paper ID: IPM-D-26-01939R1]
⚠️ Important Notice for Reviewers

This repository contains the supplementary materials for the submitted manuscript. To preserve the integrity of the double-blind review process, this repository is hosted under an anonymous account.

Contents
This repository provides the legal knowledge base used in our experiments, along with the code used to generate and validate it. Specifically, it includes:

knowledge_base/: A sample of the validated legal knowledge entries (full knowledge base available upon request or after publication).

construction/: API calling scripts for generating initial legal knowledge using LLMs (Qwen3-235B-A22B).

validation/: The evaluation rubric and validation protocol used by our legal experts.

Knowledge Base Format
Each knowledge entry is structured as:

{
  "id": "...",
  "charge_name": "...",
  "definition": "...",
  "constituent_elements": "...",
  "judicial_interpretations": "..."
}
Note: Charge names are explicitly excluded from the knowledge entries to prevent label leakage during retriever training.

Generating Knowledge Entries
To reproduce the knowledge generation process:

bash
python generate_knowledge.py --model qwen3-235b-a22b --charges charges.txt --output knowledge_raw.json
The script requires an API key for the LLM service. The prompt template used for generation is provided in prompts/prompt_template.txt.

Validated Knowledge Base
The sample entries in knowledge_base_samples/ have been validated by three legal experts following the protocol described in the manuscript (Appendix A). The validation criteria and inter-rater agreement statistics are also provided.

Contact
For questions regarding the knowledge base or the generation code, please open an issue in this repository.

Note: This is a preliminary release for review purposes. The complete knowledge base and the full model implementation will be released upon acceptance.
